":6}]}]},{"comment":"The logic here assumes that if `engineConfig.hasNested()` returns true, it sets the parent field in the index writer configuration to `ROOT_DOC_FIELD_NAME`. Ensure that this behavior is consistent with how Elasticsearch handles nested documents and that setting the parent field does not introduce any unintended side effects or performance issues.","nodes":[{"id":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/engine/InternalEngine.java-server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/engine/InternalEngine.java--139258:139360","promptId":"#RRGED","srcPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/engine/InternalEngine.java","dstPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/engine/InternalEngine.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":139258,"endPos":139360,"startLine":2732,"startLineOffset":12,"endLine":2734,"endLineOffset":13,"length":103}]}]},{"comment":"The test case has been modified to verify that index sort can be applied correctly when there are no conflicting nested fields. Additionally, a new scenario is added to ensure that an `IllegalArgumentException` is thrown when trying to apply index sort to a field within a nested object. This provides better coverage for the changes made in #N4HG7.","nodes":[{"id":"server/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/MapperServiceTests.java-server/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/MapperServiceTests.java-6391:6746,6756:6878,7064:7298,7307:7429-6391:6639,6649:6834,6843:6872,6881:6932,7118:7275,7285:7368,7377:7938,7947:8069","promptId":"#VJM77","srcPath":"server/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/MapperServiceTests.java","dstPath":"server/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/MapperServiceTests.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":6391,"endPos":6746,"startLine":129,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":135,"endLineOffset":10,"length":356},{"pos":6756,"endPos":6878,"startLine":137,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":137,"endLineOffset":130,"length":123},{"pos":7064,"endPos":7298,"startLi